/-!
# `row_residue` for q = 4 through `ZMod 23`

`vSeedPrime 4 = 23`.  Data (all checked exactly in Python, see `checks/`):
* `q4rzD r` is the lcm of the denominators of row `r` of
  `q4SourceMatrixAtZeroExplicit`; `q4rzN0 = diag(q4rzD) * M_0` and
  `q4rzAN = diag(q4rzD) * A` are integer matrices, so
  `diag(q4rzD) * M_t = q4rzN0 - t * q4rzAN`;
* for `t = 0..4`, `q4rzE * q4rzNbar_t = q4rzL_t * q4rzU_t` in `ZMod 23`, with
  `q4rzE` upper and `q4rzL_t` lower unitriangular, and `q4rzNbar_t` the residue of
  `q4rzN0 - t * q4rzAN`;
* `q4rzW` inverts the Vandermonde matrix `(tʲ)` modulo 23.

No rational determinant at `T ≠ 0`, no rational interpolation, and no 9 by 9
Leibniz expansion occurs.  Every `decide` acts on entries below 23, on one
`ℤ → ZMod 23` cast, on one 9-term dot product, or on the product of nine
small naturals.  Determinants are reached only through `Matrix.det_mul`,
`Matrix.det_of_isUpperTriangular`/`isLowerTriangular` and `RingHom.map_det`.
Exact coefficient residues: [5, 8, 16, 21, 20] = `vSeedResidueRow 4`.
-/

namespace Li2Lean.B3

noncomputable section

open Li2Lean
open Matrix

set_option maxRecDepth 1000000
set_option maxHeartbeats 20000000

instance q4rzFact : Fact (Nat.Prime (vSeedPrime 4)) := ⟨by norm_num [vSeedPrime]⟩

